meta {
  name: Update Payout Settings
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/payouts/settings
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{payoutsOwnerToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "teamBonus": {
      "enabled": false,
      "stackable": false,
      "levels": [{ "thresholdPremium": 300000, "poolAmount": 0 }],
      "csrSharePercent": 20,
      "producerSharePercent": 80
    }
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("echoes the stored section", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().teamBonus.stackable).to.equal(false);
    expect(res.getBody().teamBonus.levels).to.deep.equal([
      { thresholdPremium: 300000, poolAmount: 0 }
    ]);
    expect(res.getBody().teamBonus.csrSharePercent).to.equal(20);
    expect(res.getBody().teamBonus.producerSharePercent).to.equal(80);
  });
}

docs {
  # PATCH /payouts/settings — change the team bonus and/or Salesperson of the Month (PAC-177)

  **Module** — `payouts`. **Permission** — `agency:payouts:admin`.

  **Body** — `teamBonus`, `salespersonOfMonth`, or both; at least one. A
  section that is sent is sent **whole** (every field), so a stored section
  never mixes new levels with an old split. Numbers are JSON numbers —
  `"5000"` is refused.

  | field | rules |
  |---|---|
  | teamBonus.enabled | boolean |
  | teamBonus.stackable | boolean — every level reached pays (pools add up), or only the highest |
  | teamBonus.levels[] | `{ thresholdPremium, poolAmount }`, at most 20; at least one while `enabled`. Thresholds more than $0 and distinct; amounts in dollars, 0 – 10,000,000, two decimals. When **not** stackable a higher level may not pay a smaller pool than the one below. Stored lowest threshold first. |
  | teamBonus.csrSharePercent, producerSharePercent | 0 – 100, at most two decimals, **must add up to 100** |
  | salespersonOfMonth.enabled | boolean |
  | salespersonOfMonth.bonusAmount | dollars, as above |

  The request sends the defaults, so repeated runs leave the demo tenant
  where they found it.

  **Response `200`** — the same shape as **Get Payout Settings**.

  **Errors**
  - `400` — empty body, an unknown field (the old `thresholdPremium` /
    `poolAmount` included), a string where a number belongs, a third decimal,
    shares that do not add up to 100%, or levels the rules above refuse
    ("Add at least one team bonus level.", "Two levels have the same
    threshold.", "A higher level cannot pay less than the level below it,
    unless the levels stack."). The reason is in `errors.formErrors` /
    `errors.fieldErrors`.
  - `403` — without `agency:payouts:admin`.
}
